      "statement": "Repair get_humanize_filesize to use binary 1024-byte units and preserve the established formatting, including zero as '0 B'.",
      "source": "def get_humanize_filesize(nbytes):\n    if nbytes == 0:\n        return '0 B'\n    units = ['B', 'K', 'M', 'G', 'T']\n    size = ''\n    while int(nbytes) > 0 and units:\n        size = '%g' % round(nbytes, 1 if nbytes < 10 else 0) + ' ' + units.pop(0)\n        nbytes = nbytes / 1000\n    return size\n",
      "examples": [
        {"given": {"nbytes": 0}, "expected": "0 B"},
        {"given": {"nbytes": 1024}, "expected": "1 K"},
        {"given": {"nbytes": 1048576}, "expected": "1 M"}
      ]
